<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Commune of Novara</h1><p class="st-meta">1116 CE – 1332 CE (approx.) · capital Novara</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Piedmontese city-republic between Milan and Vercelli, caught for two centuries between its larger neighbours until absorbed by the Visconti.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Novara, an old Roman town on the road from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Milan</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a>, had a commune governed by consuls by 1116, gradually taking power from its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> and the counts of Biandrate.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The commune was governed by consuls and later a podestà. It joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lombard-league">Lombard League</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a>, but its position between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Milan</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-vercelli">Vercelli</a> made it a frequent battleground. Grain farming in its countryside and traffic on the road to the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> supported the town. In the 13th and 14th centuries the Tornielli and Brusati families led rival factions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1332 Novara submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azzone-visconti">Azzone Visconti</a> and became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-milan">Lordship of Milan</a>. It remained <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Milanese</a> until passing to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia</a> in 1738.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1116 CE – 1332 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:81.91%;width:4.30%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1116 CE – 1332 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Novara</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lombard, Piedmontese, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Novara</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1224&amp;focus=commune-of-novara" aria-label="Commune of Novara on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4885 575 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Commune of Novara lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5205 831L5218 830"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5218 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5205 831h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5205 831h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Novara. <a href="/atlas?year=1224&amp;focus=commune-of-novara">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

